cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Please cite the exact release or commit used. This is development research software, not a security-certified cryptosystem."
type: software
title: "CPWI: inverting coupled permutation-word recurrences over alternating groups"
version: 1.2.0
authors:
  - family-names: Filardo
    given-names: Gautier-Edouard
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0005-8310-2065"
    affiliation: "Efrei Research Lab, Efrei Paris Panthéon-Assas"
repository-code: "https://github.com/gautierfilardo-efrei/cpwi-post-quantum-dynamical-inversion"
url: "https://github.com/gautierfilardo-efrei/cpwi-post-quantum-dynamical-inversion"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Reference implementation and cryptanalysis of coupled permutation-word
  inversion (CPWI) over alternating groups. Includes the forward map and
  its original finite-instance diagnostics, an independent audit with
  layered state-merging inversion and collision comparators, a
  constraint-propagation solver for the single-round two-register word
  system with backward end-to-end inversion and a measured cost curve, and
  an exact bit-vector encoding solved with Z3. These materials establish
  neither classical nor post-quantum security and define no deployable
  cryptosystem.
keywords:
  - alternating groups
  - group-based cryptography
  - one-way functions
  - cryptanalysis
  - meet-in-the-middle
  - SMT solving
  - reproducibility
